Title: GREYHARBOR
Episode: 106 "Number Station"
Credit: Original fixture material written for the Canon AI test harness.

INT. WEATHER STATION - NIGHT

Rain lashes the windows. Rafi pounds on the locked door of the weather station.

RAFI
Open it!

Lila's voice crackles through the wall radio.

LILA (V.O.)
Harbor watch says you stay there until dawn. Their lock, not mine.

Rafi looks at the dead bolt from the inside. He is trapped with the instruments and the storm.

INT. EDDA'S KITCHEN - SAME NIGHT

Edda ladles chowder into two bowls. Mara sits by the stove, listening to rain hammer the roof.

Rafi sits at Edda's table, dripping rain onto the floorboards.

RAFI
The number station moved. It is using the ferry band now.

MARA
You were at the weather station.

RAFI
Weather changed.

EXT. BUS DEPOT - MORNING

A state car noses past the shuttered depot. NOLAN HALE steps out in a clean coat that hates the town already.

Mara watches from beneath the awning.

HALE
Mara Voss?

MARA
Depends who is asking.

HALE
State investigator. I hear a blue hook means your brother is alive.

HALE
That is a tidy little signal for a dead man's sister.

Mara's face closes.

INT. CLINIC BACK ROOM - DAY

Danny lies on the cot with a towel over his eyes. Gideon changes the bandage on Danny's ribs with surprising care.

DANNY
You learn that on the ferry?

GIDEON
You learn it losing fights.

MARA
Hale knows about the blue hook.

Danny sits up too fast and coughs.

DANNY
Then whoever fed him has been close enough to touch our pockets.

EXT. CANNERY YARD - DUSK

Lila follows a trail of wet boot prints through the canning yard. The prints end at a locked freezer door.

Inside, a radio clicks once.

VOICE ON RADIO
Thursday. Osprey. South teeth.

Lila backs away.

INT. HARBORMASTER'S OFFICE - NIGHT

Hale sits at Tobias's desk without asking. Mara stays standing.

HALE
Cole Brannigan died inconveniently.

MARA
For him, mostly.

HALE
For everybody who needed him to explain the ledger.

MARA
You found the ledger?

HALE
I found people frightened of it.

EXT. BREAKWATER - NIGHT

The sea is black glass. Danny stands where Cole died and listens.

Far out, with no buoy to warn it, a boat scrapes the rocks.

Danny hears men shouting and then one clean bell note from nowhere.

FADE OUT.
